  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Operational Roadmaps on Regional Value Chains in Sub-Saharan Africa - Phase II Study</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;Under the value chain diagnostic project for the African Continent commissioned by the European Commission&#xbf;s (EC) INTPA-A1 and the African Union Commission DG ETTIM, ITC identified 94 promising value chains with potential for regionalisation and for increasing intra-African trade by fostering value addition on the continent.. For an initial four of these promising value chains, notably pharmaceuticals, automotive, apparel of cotton and formulated complementary foods (FCF) for older infants and young children (6-23 months) use, additional work on identifying barriers to developing these and private sector needs in terms of skills, investment, and technologies, has been carried out and is documented in the ITC-AU-EU publication entitled &#xbf;Made by Africa &#xbf; Creating value through integration&#xbf;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Within the framework of the Continental Component of the &quot;Africa Trade Competitiveness and Market Access Programme&quot;, ITC will build on the aggregate insights from the phase I &quot;diagnsotic Made by Africa&quot; and contributions received from EU delegations in SSA, to deepen the diagnostics, engage with relevant actors from the EU and local private sector, financial sector and public authorities and come up with concrete ideas in the shape of operational roadmaps for building 2 pilot Global Gateway projects for each of the three value chains &#xbf; the automotive ecosystem notably on e-vehicles, Formulated Complementary Food (FCF) and pharmaceuticals. For each value chain, it will focus on a limited set of specific countries and sub-regions identified in the results of the mapping exercises led by the EC, or depending on findings deemed of relevance and assessed with EC INTPA E2 during the course of the study.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
